sections.text:
The combined optimal planning challenge of identifying the optimal placement and
sizing of EVCS, DGs, and CBs in radial distribution networks is the focus of this study to
verify the following:
1. Reduce power losses, including active and reactive;
2. Improve voltage stability and voltage profiles;
3. Uphold operating restrictions (power balance, temperature limits, and voltage limitations);
4. Assess system performance at different EV penetration levels (30%, 40%, and 50%);
5. Reduce annual CO 2 emissions;
6. Assure the interpretability of the answer and computational efficiency.
